  <diagram id="uc28b_assignchangemeetingrole" name="UC-28b - Manage Meeting Role &amp; Additional Permissions">
    <mxGraphModel grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="0" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <UserObject id="mermaid-uc28b_assignchangemeetingrole" label="" mermaidData="{&quot;data&quot;: &quot;%%{init: {\&quot;sequence\&quot;: {\&quot;mirrorActors\&quot;: false}}}%%\nsequenceDiagram\nactor User as \&quot;Secretary\&quot;\nparticipant MeetingPage@{ \&quot;type\&quot;: \&quot;boundary\&quot; } as \&quot;Meeting Management Page\&quot;\nparticipant ParticipantController@{ \&quot;type\&quot;: \&quot;control\&quot; } as \&quot;:Meeting Participant Controller\&quot;\nparticipant ParticipantService@{ \&quot;type\&quot;: \&quot;control\&quot; } as \&quot;:Meeting Participant Service\&quot;\nparticipant ParticipantRepository as \&quot;:Meeting Participant Repository\&quot;\nparticipant Database@{ \&quot;type\&quot;: \&quot;database\&quot; } as \&quot;:Database\&quot;\nparticipant NotificationService as \&quot;:Notification Service\&quot;\nUser-&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: Submit role/permission changes, including confirmed Chair replacement when applicable\nactivate MeetingPage\nMeetingPage-&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: Submit role/permission changes, including confirmed Chair replacement when applicable\nactivate ParticipantController\nParticipantController-&gt;&gt;ParticipantService: manageMeetingRoleAndPermissions(meeting, secretary, participant, changes, replacementConfirmation)\nactivate ParticipantService\nParticipantService-&gt;&gt;ParticipantRepository: Read Meeting status, current internal and Guest roster,&lt;br/&gt;actor relationship, roles and additional permissions\nactivate ParticipantRepository\nParticipantRepository-&gt;&gt;Database: Retrieve current Meeting and roster information\nactivate Database\nDatabase--&gt;&gt;ParticipantRepository: Current information / Read failure\ndeactivate Database\nParticipantRepository--&gt;&gt;ParticipantService: Current information / Read failure\ndeactivate ParticipantRepository\nParticipantService-&gt;&gt;ParticipantService: Verify current Secretary, current internal participant or Guest invitation, editable status,&lt;br/&gt;valid role and permitted extras (BR-79, BR-80, BR-85, BR-174, BR-175)\nalt Secretary or selected internal/Guest participant is no longer current - EX-2\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: Request denied; all roles and permissions unchanged\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: Request denied; all roles and permissions unchanged\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: Request denied; all roles and permissions unchanged\nelse Meeting status disallows changes - EX-2\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: MSG98 - The meeting participant list cannot be modified in its current status.\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: MSG98 - The meeting participant list cannot be modified in its current status.\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: MSG98 - The meeting participant list cannot be modified in its current status.\nelse Internal role is invalid or a Guest role change is requested - EX-1\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: MSG101 - A valid meeting role is required.\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: MSG101 - A valid meeting role is required.\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: MSG101 - A valid meeting role is required.\nelse Requested grant is invalid under the agreed permission policy - EX-1\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: MSG152 - One or more selected meeting permissions are not allowed.\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: MSG152 - One or more selected meeting permissions are not allowed.\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: MSG152 - One or more selected meeting permissions are not allowed.\nelse Published/InProgress last Secretary would be lost without same-save replacement,\\na second Chair created, or required current Chair removed - EX-1\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: MSG109 - The meeting must retain its required Chair and Secretary. Assign a replacement first.\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: MSG109 - The meeting must retain its required Chair and Secretary. Assign a replacement first.\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: MSG109 - The meeting must retain its required Chair and Secretary. Assign a replacement first.\nelse Meeting is Published or InProgress, the Chair account is active and the change replaces the current Chair,\\ngives the Chair role to another participant or changes the Chair to another role - EX-5\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: MSG256 - From publication onward, only the current Chair can hand over the Chair role while the Chair account is active.\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: MSG256 - From publication onward, only the current Chair can hand over the Chair role while the Chair account is active.\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: MSG256 - From publication onward, only the current Chair can hand over the Chair role while the Chair account is active.\nelse Requested change is valid\nalt Confirmed replacement of the current Chair before publication, or after publication when the Chair account is locked - AF-1\nParticipantService-&gt;&gt;ParticipantService: Recheck Meeting is not yet Published or the Chair account is locked, outgoing Chair&lt;br/&gt;and incoming current active internal participant (not the Secretary after publication); exactly one Chair;&lt;br/&gt;preparation may temporarily have no Secretary (BR-122, BR-123, BR-126, BR-169, BR-294, BR-295)\nParticipantService-&gt;&gt;ParticipantRepository: Change outgoing Chair to Member and incoming participant to Chair together;&lt;br/&gt;combine role defaults and valid individual grants; no hardcoded two-view ceiling;&lt;br/&gt;preserve system roles and responses (BR-169, BR-177)\nactivate ParticipantRepository\nParticipantRepository-&gt;&gt;Database: Save all requested changes together;&lt;br/&gt;recheck Meeting status, authority and roster before saving\nactivate Database\nDatabase--&gt;&gt;ParticipantRepository: Complete save / No changes saved\ndeactivate Database\nParticipantRepository--&gt;&gt;ParticipantService: Complete save / No changes saved\ndeactivate ParticipantRepository\nelse Standard internal role/permission change or Guest permission-only change - AF-2\nParticipantService-&gt;&gt;ParticipantRepository: Save permitted internal role/permission changes or Guest additional Meeting permissions;&lt;br/&gt;preserve system role and invitation response (BR-86, BR-96, BR-177)\nactivate ParticipantRepository\nParticipantRepository-&gt;&gt;Database: Save all requested changes together;&lt;br/&gt;recheck Meeting status, authority and roster before saving\nactivate Database\nDatabase--&gt;&gt;ParticipantRepository: Complete save / No changes saved\ndeactivate Database\nParticipantRepository--&gt;&gt;ParticipantService: Complete save / No changes saved\ndeactivate ParticipantRepository\nend\nalt Update cannot be completed - EX-3\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: MSG102 - Unable to update the meeting role. Please try again.\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: MSG102 - Unable to update the meeting role. Please try again.\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: MSG102 - Unable to update the meeting role. Please try again.\nelse Complete change saved\nopt Meeting is Published or InProgress\nParticipantService-&gt;&gt;NotificationService: Notify affected internal participants or Guest by email;&lt;br/&gt;the actor gets no in-app notification (BR-92, BR-94, BR-322)\nactivate NotificationService\nNotificationService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantService: Delivery arranged / Failure recorded for retry\ndeactivate NotificationService\nend\nalt Meeting role changed\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: MSG100 - Meeting role updated successfully.\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: MSG100 - Meeting role updated successfully.\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: MSG100 - Meeting role updated successfully.\nelse Only additional permissions changed\nParticipantService--&gt;&gt;ParticipantController: MSG153 - Meeting permissions updated successfully.\nParticipantController--&gt;&gt;MeetingPage: MSG153 - Meeting permissions updated successfully.\nMeetingPage--&gt;&gt;User: MSG153 - Meeting permissions updated successfully.\nend\nend\nend\ndeactivate ParticipantService\ndeactivate ParticipantController\ndeactivate MeetingPage&quot;, &quot;config&quot;: null}">
          <mxCell connectable="0" parent="1" vertex="1" style="group;transparentBounds=1;editIcon=1;lockedGroup=0;groupPadding=20;">
            <mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="3787.0" height="46.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
